        "original_id": "50f4a24c-9fa4-52ec-a294-1b49e1443b42",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Louise, Le roi malgré lui, Julien\n- People: Gustave Charpentier, Saint-Pol-Roux, Emmanuel Chabrier, Emile de Najac, Paul Burani\n- Concepts: opera, opéra-comique, libretto, sequel\n\nFacts:\n- In 1887, Emmanuel Chabrier’s Le roi malgré lui was composed as an opéra-comique in three acts with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\n- In 1900, Gustave Charpentier’s Louise was an opera described as a “roman musical” in four acts with an original French libretto by Charpentier.\n- Saint-Pol-Roux, a symbolist poet and an inspiration for the surrealists, contributed to the libretto of Louise.\n- Julien is a sequel to Gustave Charpentier’s Louise and portrays the artistic aspirations of Louise’s suitor Julien.",
